Research Experience
Computational Biology Intern May 2026 – Sept 2026
Protein Engineering Group, AB Biosciences Concord, MA
• Predicted 500+ antibody-fusion structures via AlphaFold3 for oncology drug discovery programs, including afucosylated
antibodies engineered for enhanced Fc effector function (ADCC) and multi-Fc/multi-Fab formats.
• Validated structural integrity via ChimeraX, optimized linkers and domain packing for stable assembly, and identified
designs to advance the company’s immunology-focused protein engineering and drug discovery pipeline.
• Benchmarked AlphaFold3 vs. ESMFold2 and authored a company-wide, SOP-style reproducibility guide for 3D predictions.
Computational Biology Researcher Oct 2022 – Aug 2025
Structural Biology Dept, Jacobs School of Medicine & Biomedical Sciences Buffalo, NY
• Processed & unified 100+ public KLF4 ChIP-seq samples to create a comprehensive data compendium.
• Aligned sequencing data and identified 50+ regulatory (e.g., nucleosome, histone, motif) determinants.
• Discovered pioneer TF factors by applying ML techniques to integrated genomic & chromatin data.
• Built a ML classifier integrating 50+ regulatory features to predict Yamanaka transcription factor binding.
• Benchmarked 3D protein prediction CASP output by comparing structural decoys against native structures.
• Enhanced accuracy of SCRMshaw ML regulatory enhancer discovery tool by varying heterochromatin evaluations.
Genomics Research Assistant May 2024 – May 2025
Biological Sciences Dept, University at Buffalo Buffalo, NY
• Developed custom Bash/UNIX scripts for the reproducible assembly of high-quality razorback sucker fish genomes.
• Executed Nanopore library preparation & DNA extraction for initial QC & downstream assembly.
• Optimized and troubleshot genomic assembly tools for parallel execution on a SLURM-managed HPC.
Biostatistics Research Intern May 2022 – Aug 2022
Columbia University New York, NY
• Analyzed ABCD study data investigating maternal substance use and adolescent neurodevelopment.
• Employed inferential statistics on high-dimensional cohort data to summarize significant findings.
